# Charie environment configuration - TEMPLATE ONLY.
#
# This file lists every configuration variable Charie reads, with safe
# placeholder values. It is documentation, not a loaded config file:
#
# - Charie never reads a .env file automatically, and no real .env file
#   may be committed. Set these variables in your shell before starting
#   the apps, or in your hosting platform's environment settings.
# - The engine also resolves the model secrets from Google Cloud Secret
#   Manager (same names) when you run with Google Cloud credentials:
#   environment wins first, Secret Manager second, no key file anywhere.
# - Every variable is OPTIONAL. With none set, the full product runs in
#   honestly labelled heuristic mode (see README, Judges quickstart).
#
# Windows PowerShell example:
#   $env:META_API_KEY="your_meta_api_key_here"
# Linux / macOS example:
#   export META_API_KEY=your_meta_api_key_here

# --- Meta Model API (unlocks Spark, Wonder, Image, Voice, SAM) ---
# Get your own key at https://dev.meta.ai (Model API). Judges: use your
# own key - never ask for, and never accept, someone else's.
META_API_KEY=your_meta_api_key_here
META_API_BASE_URL=https://api.meta.ai/v1
META_SPARK_MODEL=muse-spark-1.3
META_WONDER_MODEL=muse-wonder-1.0
META_IMAGE_MODEL=muse-image-1.0
META_VOICE_MODEL=muse-voice-transcribe-1.0
META_SAM_MODEL=sam-3-1

# --- Baseten (Muse Spark Open, open weights) - optional ---
# The Chat/Meet default brain when set. Not required for judging.
BASETEN_API_KEY=your_baseten_api_key_here
SPARK_OPEN_MODEL_ID=meta-models/muse-spark-open-1026
SPARK_OPEN_ENDPOINT=https://inference.baseten.co/v1

# --- Muse Glimmer triage (open weights, Ollama by default) - optional ---
GLIMMER_ENDPOINT=http://localhost:11434/v1
GLIMMER_MODEL=muse-glimmer:30b
GLIMMER_API_KEY=

# --- Charie voice: Cartesia Sonic (third-party TTS, optional) ---
# Primary call voice when set: sub-second first audio, conversational.
# Muse Spark stays the brain; TTS is interchangeable. Get a key at
# cartesia.ai, pick any voice (or leave the default), and set both on
# the PORTAL (not the engine). Without it, Modal Kokoro below is used,
# then the browser voice.
CARTESIA_API_KEY=
CARTESIA_VOICE_ID=
CARTESIA_MODEL=sonic-2

# --- Charie voice on Modal (Kokoro) - optional fallback ---
# Deploy services/modal-tts/modal_app.py and paste the printed URL.
# This is your Modal endpoint, not a credential. Without it, calls use
# the browser voice.
CHARIE_TTS_URL=https://your-workspace--charie-tts-speak.modal.run
CHARIE_TTS_MODAL_KEY=
CHARIE_TTS_MODAL_SECRET=

# --- Portal <-> engine wiring ---
ENGINE_URL=http://localhost:3103
ENGINE_TOKEN=choose_a_long_random_token_for_local_use
# Local-only bypass for the engine token check (never use hosted):
ENGINE_DEV_OPEN=1

# --- Portal auth and storage ---
# SESSION_KEY must be at least 16 characters; in hosted Firestore mode
# the portal refuses to sign sessions without it.
SESSION_KEY=choose_a_long_random_session_key_32_chars
AUTOMATION_KEY=
CRON_KEY=
PORTAL_STORE=
FIREBASE_WEB_CONFIG=
NEXT_PUBLIC_VAPID_PUBLIC=
VAPID_PUBLIC=
VAPID_PRIVATE=

# --- Google Cloud (optional: Secret Manager, Firestore, GCS, log watch) ---
GCP_PROJECT_ID=your_project_id_here
GOOGLE_CLOUD_PROJECT=your_project_id_here
GCS_BUCKET=
# GOOGLE_APPLICATION_CREDENTIALS=/path/to/application-default-credentials.json

# --- Misc ---
PORTAL_PUBLIC_URL=http://localhost:3102
PORTAL_URL=http://localhost:3102
ENGINE_PUBLIC_URL=http://localhost:3103
RECALL_API_KEY=
